{"nodes": [{"id": "vault_system_how_glue_works", "label": "GLUE: how it works now (SYSTEM)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read first. Says how GLUE works today, in one place; the ADRs say why. A change that alters anything in it updates this file in the same commit."}, {"id": "vault_system_scratch_platter", "label": "Prepare vinyl scrubbing in the website (scratch engine and platter)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "scratch.svelte.ts plus platter.ts: the Prepare deck's vinyl scrubbing, a second audio path while the deck is held (ADR 0192)."}, {"id": "vault_system_main_dj_library", "label": "The main DJ library (GLUE 0.66)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One per computer (Source.main), kept through every read. A song's BPM is GLUE's correction, then the main library's grid, then the analysis (bpmInUse). Its grid and cues are GLUE's own, else the main library's (lib/cues.ts mainOf, prepare.grid). The two-way sync is with it (ADR 0169)."}, {"id": "vault_system_cues_grids_from_every_app", "label": "Cues, loops and beat grids from every DJ app (GLUE 0.65)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each record keeps its cues, loops and grid (SourceTrack.cueList, grid); Engine DJ's come from PerformanceData (enginePerf.ts, glue_interop::perf). Prepare shows each app's and takes them on a click. GLUE writes into a DJ app's library only as ADR 0168 allows: through GLUE Home, opt-in per library, backup first, app closed; not yet in this release."}, {"id": "vault_system_engine_dj_kept_in_step", "label": "Engine DJ kept in step both ways (GLUE 0.67)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hot cues, saved loops and grid merged three ways per song against what they last agreed on; PerformanceData written only while Engine DJ and its analyser are not running, after a copy (dj-backups/, one per close, the last 3 kept, ADR 0173). Engine DJ's changes are taken into prep as the song's own edit. Clashes are settled in Prepare (djClashes, djResolve) (ADR 0170)."}], "edges": [{"source": "vault_system_scratch_platter", "target": "vault_adr_0192_vinyl_scrubbing_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_scratch_platter", "target": "src_lib_scratch_svelte", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_scratch_platter", "target": "src_lib_platter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_main_dj_library", "target": "vault_adr_0169_the_main_dj_library_decision", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_main_dj_library", "target": "src_lib_cues", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "vault/SYSTEM.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "vault_system_cues_grids_from_every_app", "target": "vault_adr_0168_dj_apps_synced_both_ways_decision", "relation": 